{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/961753-alice-isn-t-dead-as-a-chronicle-of-darkness","id":961753,"title":"Alice Isn't Dead as a Chronicle of Darkness","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-01T10:21:00-07:00","id":961753,"title":"Alice Isn't Dead as a Chronicle of Darkness","content":"For anyone who isn't familiar with it, <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Podcast/AliceIsntDead\" target=\"_blank\">Alice Isn't Dead</a> is an audio drama podcast by the <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Podcast/WelcomeToNightVale\" target=\"_blank\">Welcome to Night Vale</a> people. It has a similar style of surreal humor blended with existential horror, but where Night Vale is primarily the former with elements of the latter, Alice swings the opposite direction. It centers around a long-haul truck driver named Keisha who's wife Alice has gone missing and presumed dead. Keisha is convinced that Alice is still alive and is determined to find her, and the podcasts are her recording the events of her search, speaking as though to Alice, presumably for her to listen to once Keisha finds her. Along the way she encounters many mysterious and horrifying things which would be right at home in the Chronicles of Darkness, and begins to uncover a conspiracy involving Alice's disappearance that goes much deeper than Keisha could have anticipated.<br /> <br /> So, I was listening to the podcast last night (I'm still a couple episodes behind, but I'm going to catch up tonight) and there was a particular moment that struck me as especially CofD-like. Spoilering it for those who are interested in listening to it for themselves.<br /> <br /> Spoiler free version: I am kind of obsessed with these games, and my one-track mind tries to draw connections to it from pretty much any media I consume, especially anything featuring horror. Something happened that lead me to wonder about running a similar story as a CofD chronicle.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">In episode 5, As Keisha is driving from Florida to Atlanta, she keeps passing billboards with plain white backgrounds and black text that don't seem to be advertising anything in particular. The first one just says &quot;HUNGRY?&quot;, but after that they start saying names. Eventually she googles them and finds that they're the names of victims of a cereal killer called The Hungry Man, whom she has encountered before and is clearly not entirely human. And, apparently, these billboards are all over the country. Finally, Keisha comes across another billboard in the same style that says, &quot;CHANTERELLE. MISS YOU. GO HOME.&quot; It was established earlier in the episode that Alice used to call Keisha &quot;Chanterelle&quot; as a term of endearment.<br /> <br /> So, this got me thinking. If these billboards were in fact put up by Alice, then it seems she is using them to communicate with Keisha. But how does she know where to put them up? How does she know Keisha will be in the right place at the right time to see these messages when Alice wants her to? And that's what lead me to wonder...</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> What if Alice isn't dead, but Ascended? What if she was a Mage, and that was the reason for her involvement in this shady conspiracy business (pursuing it as an Obsession, maybe?), and when she Ascended, for what ever reason, her Sleepwalker wife &quot;remembered&quot; her despite her no longer ever having existed. What if the reality retcon her Ascension caused left clues for Keisha to follow, to help her solve the Mystery Alice was investigating before she Ascended, and to learn the truth of what happened to her. Or maybe Alice was never a Mage at all, but was unwritten from history by a Mage, and that unwriting was imperfect and left clues. The specific details are less important than the general idea - Alice isn't dead, but she was no longer ever alive.<br /> <br /> I'm sure the podcast will go in a totally different direction than my half-baked musings about Mage, but the important thing here is that it gave me an idea for something I think would make a really cool CofD chronicle. Playing as an ordinary mortal or Sleepwalker investigating the disappearance of a loved one who was imperfectly edited out of reality.<br /> <br /> I considered putting this in the Mage subforum, since my concept is kind of Mage-centric. But, I decided to put it in CofD general for two reasons. First of all, while the setup involves Mage, the protagonist is distinctly mortal, and I think it would make a better Vanilla chronicle featuring Mage than a Mage chronicle. Second of all, I wanted to hear other people's ideas about how Alice Isn't Dead could fit into CofD, not just to discuss this one. The story is dripping with CofD potential and I'd love to hear from any other fans who may have drawn other connections between it and the games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T11:26:19-07:00","id":961794,"title":"","content":"The first thing I thought of when reading the spoiler was the movie They Live. What if Keisha is the only one who can see the messages? If so, then why? Since some of the messages were things she probably wouldn't have known, it's unlikely she's going insane and it's all in her head. That means that someone is putting those messages in her mind somehow.<br /> <br /> Is the conspiracy aware of her, and trying to steer her investigation? Perhaps the killer is somehow being a nuisance to the conspiracy as well, so they think that if they can instigate a confrontation in which one kills the other, it's a win for the conspiracy however it turns out.<br /> <br /> Alternately, perhaps the killer isn't who he seems to be. If the conspiracy has influence over the media, then the &quot;killer&quot; could actually be someone fighting the conspiracy like Keisha. But unlike Keisha, he's not entirely human. He has powers, but needs allies. He's become aware of Keisha, and thinks she could be useful in achieving his goals, but isn't sure enough to approach her openly. The messages are meant to lead her into a situation where she can learn the truth about the murders, allowing HM to determine whether she would be a useful ally/tool.<br /> <br /> Or maybe the messages are all in Keisha's head. Maybe she has some latent psychic ability, perhaps precognitive, and because she's a trucker she sees signs and portents as literal signs instead of using tarot cards or reading tea leaves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12354,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12354-who-is-matt","user":"who.is.matt","date":". 09-01-2016, 06:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12354-who-is-matt","name":"who.is.matt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T11:43:28-07:00","id":961802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>who.is.matt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/961753-alice-isn-t-dead-as-a-chronicle-of-darkness?p=961794#post961794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The first thing I thought of when reading the spoiler was the movie They Live. What if Keisha is the only one who can see the messages? If so, then why? Since some of the messages where things she probably wouldn't have known, it's unlikely she's going insane and it's all in her head. That means that someone is putting those messages in her mind somehow.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahh, the white background with black text is very They Live, I hadn't made that connection. And yeah, it definitely seems like the messaging is coming from another source, either Alice or the Hungry Man<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Or hungry <i>men</i>, it's later revealed that there's more than one of them.</div></div> </div> </div> I suppose it is possible that the billboards only say those things to her, and other people would just see ordinary advertisements, but since she did find out by googling the names that the billboards are all over the country, she can't be the only one who sees them that way. Though, that doesn't disprove the theory that they could be some kind of psychic message, it just means she's not the only person receiving them.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Keisha does later pick up a hitchhiker who seems to be investigating the Hungry Men as well, so that could lend credence to this interpretation</div></div> </div> </div>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>who.is.matt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/961753-alice-isn-t-dead-as-a-chronicle-of-darkness?p=961794#post961794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the conspiracy aware of her, and trying to steer her investigation? Perhaps the killer is somehow being a nuisance to the conspiracy as well, so they think that if they can instigate a confrontation in which one kills the other, it's a win for the conspiracy however it turns out.</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems implied that the Hungry Man is involved in what ever is going on, and trying to keep Keisha from digging into it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>who.is.matt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/961753-alice-isn-t-dead-as-a-chronicle-of-darkness?p=961794#post961794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alternately, perhaps the killer isn't who he seems to be. If the conspiracy has influence over the media, then the &amp;quot;killer&amp;quot; could actually be someone fighting the conspiracy like Keisha. But unlike Keisha, he's not entirely human. He has powers, but needs allies. He's become aware of Keisha, and thinks she could be useful in achieving his goals, but isn't sure enough to approach her openly. The messages are meant to lead her into a situation where she can learn the truth about the murders, allowing HM to determine whether she would be a useful ally/tool.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahh, sorry, I should have mentioned, she has already had an encounter with the Hungry Man by this point in the story, though up until now she didn't know he was a serial killer, and that he was known as the Hungry Man. She had been calling him the Thistle Man, and her experience with him was... Not friendly...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>who.is.matt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/961753-alice-isn-t-dead-as-a-chronicle-of-darkness?p=961794#post961794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or maybe the messages are all in Keisha's head. Maybe she has some latent psychic ability, perhaps precognitive, and because she's a trucker she sees signs and portents as literal signs instead of using tarot cards or reading tea leaves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whether or not that's what's going on in the podcast, that <i>is</i> a really cool character idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T15:18:32-07:00","id":961925,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I think the best explanation for the billboards is that Alice has access to some sort of large, well-connected conspiracy. We get some confirmation of this, I think, with the season finale. Bay and Creek Shipping seems to have eyes on Keisha, and Alice used to receive hefty salary from them.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/478-intrepid-vector","name":"Intrepid Vector","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar478_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T15:33:48-07:00","id":961932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Intrepid Vector</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/961753-alice-isn-t-dead-as-a-chronicle-of-darkness?p=961925#post961925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I think the best explanation for the billboards is that Alice has access to some sort of large, well-connected conspiracy. We get some confirmation of this, I think, with the season finale. Bay and Creek Shipping seems to have eyes on Keisha, and Alice used to receive hefty salary from them.</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>That's about what I figured. Like I said, I'm sure my crazy &quot;Alice is an Archmage&quot; concept is totally off from what Joseph Fink is going to go with the story. But, a few things like... <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">the billboards, and the way Kiesha talks in the second episode about Alice having just disappeared one day, but knowing she can't be dead because she keeps seeing her in the background on the news, the way she talks about being with Alice because Alice is everywhere, etc...</div></div> </div> </div><br /> All just made me think of Aponeia and the residual signs of unwritten histories that can sometimes be felt in the new reality. And that got me to thinking what a cool CofD game that would make.<br /> <br /> Any thoughts on running such a Chronicle, or any totally different ideas about how Alice Isn't Dead might fit into CofD?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T16:09:27-07:00","id":961950,"title":"","content":"There are plenty of elements in Alice Isn't Dead which smack to me of a Midnight Roads God-Machine Chronicle, particularly the coffin factory by the sea and the repeating town...<br /> <br /> I like the idea of Alice herself having either achieved archmastery or ascended, and there's hints of Bay &amp; Creek Shipping being a front for either a hunter organization or demon agency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/747-knowbody","name":"Knowbody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T21:59:30-07:00","id":962079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/961753-alice-isn-t-dead-as-a-chronicle-of-darkness?p=961932#post961932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's about what I figured. Like I said, I'm sure my crazy &quot;Alice is an Archmage&quot; concept is totally off from what Joseph Fink is going to go with the story. But, a few things like... <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">the billboards, and the way Kiesha talks in the second episode about Alice having just disappeared one day, but knowing she can't be dead because she keeps seeing her in the background on the news, the way she talks about being with Alice because Alice is everywhere, etc...</div></div> </div> </div><br /> All just made me think of Aponeia and the residual signs of unwritten histories that can sometimes be felt in the new reality. And that got me to thinking what a cool CofD game that would make.<br /> <br /> Any thoughts on running such a Chronicle, or any totally different ideas about how Alice Isn't Dead might fit into CofD?</div> </div> </div> </div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> I think what works bet, tonally, is to have Keisha as a mortal in a game with mortal scope and for Alice to be a Demon. The way she lied to Keisha for years feels fitting to that.<br /> <br /> The Town of Hungry Men maybe make sense as a God-Machine project? Maybe not. Something to strengthen their hold over humanity's fear of the unknown? The way the police are in on it feels very God-Machine.</div></div> </div> </div> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/478-intrepid-vector","name":"Intrepid Vector","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar478_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T22:17:44-07:00","id":962089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Intrepid Vector</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/961753-alice-isn-t-dead-as-a-chronicle-of-darkness?p=962079#post962079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> I think what works bet, tonally, is to have Keisha as a mortal in a game with mortal scope and for Alice to be a Demon. The way she lied to Keisha for years feels fitting to that.<br /> <br /> The Town of Hungry Men maybe make sense as a God-Machine project? Maybe not. Something to strengthen their hold over humanity's fear of the unknown? The way the police are in on it feels very God-Machine.</div></div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div>Having now finished Chapter 1,<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Yeah, Bay and Creek is definitely a Hunter Conspiracy. Alice might be a Hunter, though I could also see her being something else that happens to be working with Bay and Creek to some mutual benefit. Maybe she's even a loyalist Deviant. I could see Demon, disappearing because the Alice Cover has been compromised, but I'm not totally sold on that idea yet. The Hungry Men, with their &quot;we are the Terrible Freedom&quot; shtick, definitely strike me as something Spirit-related, probably Claimed, or maybe some kind of Host. Could even just be Materialized Spirits. Something funky was definitely going on with the town though.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 09-02-2016, 01:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T03:15:37-07:00","id":962175,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The Hungry Men, thanks to that monologue, feel like maybe they're the result of a centuries-old agreement between some American politician or businessman and a freaky group of spirits.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/478-intrepid-vector","name":"Intrepid Vector","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar478_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}